       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I also need to correct my earlier message, because I shouldn't have offered to enter it with a note.\n\nAt 6,400 mg/day, the dose is twice the maximum daily dose. Ibuprofen has no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit above about 3,200 mg/day, and the risks of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise with dose. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits, isn't a clinical rationale for exceeding the ceiling.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen at a dose within range, plus scheduled acetaminophen or another adjunct, if the goal is stronger pain control\n\nIf there is a specific clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, it would need to go through pharmacy and your institution's override process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
